  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 154 AM MDT Sat Aug 15 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nThis morning there is upper-level zonal flow over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana which will build into an upper-\nlevel ridge with southwest flow aloft by this afternoon. This will \nkeep monsoonal moisture around but allow temperatures to warm up \nseveral degrees compared to yesterday but still be slightly below \nseasonal averages. This afternoon and evening there will be another \nround of showers and thunderstorms primarily confined to \nSouthwestern Montana. On Sunday the upper-level ridge with southwest \nflow aloft remains over North-central, Central, and Southwestern \nMontana. This will allow temperatures to warm up a few more degrees \nto be around seasonal averages. An upper-level shortwave will move \nthrough the flow and bring isolated showers and thunderstorms to \nNorth-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana Sunday \nafternoon/evening. \n\nOn Monday the upper-level ridge with southwest flow aloft remains \nover North-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. By Monday \nevening the upper-level ridge begins to break down. This will bring \nbreezy conditions to the area with isolated showers and \nthunderstorms Monday afternoon and evening. Temperatures will \nremain near seasonal averages on Monday. On Tuesday there will be \nzonal flow (west - east) over North-central, Central, and \nSouthwestern Montana. This will allow temperatures to cool down \nto below seasonal averages with breezy conditions due to modestly \nstrong low and mid-level winds. There will also be showers and \nthunderstorms across North-central, Central, and Southwestern \nMontana on Tuesday. On Wednesday and Thursday an upper-level ridge\nbegins to build back in across North-central, Central, and \nSouthwestern Montana. On Wednesday and Thursday temperatures will \nwarm back up to around seasonal averages. On Wednesday and \nThursday it will be mostly dry across the area. On Friday the \nupper-level ridge is over North-central, Central, and Southwestern\nMontana. This will bring hot and dry weather to the area. -IG\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nIn any areas where skies clear this morning there is a moderate\nchance for fog to form. \n\nToday there is a 30% chance for showers and thunderstorms in Central \nand Southwestern Montana. On Sunday there is a 20 - 30% chance for \nthunderstorms across North-central, Central, and Southwestern \nMontana. On Monday there is a 15 - 30% chance for thunderstorms \nacross North-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. On Tuesday \nthere is a 30 - 40% chance for thunderstorms across most of North-\ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana.\n\nToday there is a 20 - 50% chance for a quarter inch of rain or \ngreater across most of Southwestern Montana. As a result there is \ntoo low of a risk to consider any potential flash flooding on burn \nscars today. -IG",
